    "abstract": "The most significant events of progress for the fall and winter of 1929–30 have been the increased production of feature pictures combining sound and color, and the marked improvement in sound quality and in picture artistry. The technical quality of color pictures, however, still leaves much to be desired and further improvements must be made before the full benefit of color will be realized.",
